CHSolitaire
Copyright 2026 bateske

From CHPoker and CHBlackjack (https://github.com/bateske/CHPoker,
https://github.com/bateske/CHBlackjack, Apache-2.0): the card face (the
ranks, pips and court portraits in the repository's tools/art/common/), the
palette, the sound sequencer, flash saving and the PC simulator. CHBlackjack
is a derivative of
"Blackjack" for the Arduboy by Press Play On Tape - Simon Holmes (filmote),
code, and Stephane C (vampirics), art - Apache-2.0
(https://github.com/Press-Play-On-Tape/Blackjack, commit 72a6b1b). From it
come the card drawing (PlayGameState_Render.cpp drawCard()), the 5x6 suit
glyphs (tools/art/common/suits.txt) and the 3x5 pixel font in the CHGame library
(platform/board/arduino/CHGame/libraries/CHGame/src/chgame/Draw.cpp).

From CHChess (https://github.com/bateske/CHChess, Apache-2.0): the input and
frame pacing (now in the CHGame library,
platform/board/arduino/CHGame/libraries/CHGame/src/chgame/Input.*), drawing primitives, outlined
lettering, effects, the pointing glove (tools/art/common/hand.*), the setup-screen
choices, the debug protocol and the simulator's script driver.

The game itself follows the rules, the scoring and the manners of the
Solitaire that came with Microsoft Windows; no code or art of it is used.
The card backs (tools/art/backs/) and the title lettering (tools/art/logo.txt,
first rendered from the Georgia typeface by tools/make_logo.py) were drawn
for this game.

Everything else - the rules, the table and its presentation, the cascade and
the screens - is new, under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE).
